cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FreshCuff ScanMade or the FreshCuff geometry in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "FreshCuff ScanMade: custom 3D-printable assistive hand cuffs from hand scans, in the browser"
abstract: >-
  FreshCuff ScanMade reads a 3D scan of a hand, compares the knuckle band with the seven
  standard sizes of the FreshCuff assistive cuff, and, for hands in the custom range,
  generates a cuff whose spring follows the back of the hand. It runs entirely in the
  browser (Pyodide); the scan never leaves the user's computer. Experimental: geometry
  checked in CAD only, not yet validated on a real wearer.
authors:
